<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf Schulten</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a>–<a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf Schulten was a German historian and archaeologist of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. From 1905 he excavated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numantia">Numantia</a>, uncovering the Celtiberian town and the ring of camps and walls built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-aemilianus">Scipio Aemilianus</a> for the siege of 134–133 BCE, which he published in a multi-volume study. He also searched for the legendary city of Tartessos and wrote widely on the Roman conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The excavations of <b>Adolf Schulten</b> from 1905 uncovered the Roman siege camps around the town, which remain among the best known Roman siege works anywhere.</blockquote><a href="/empire/celtiberians">Celtiberians · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Adolf Schulten</b> thought the city might lie buried in the wetlands near the river's mouth, now the Doñana National Park.</blockquote><a href="/culture/tartessos">Tartessos · Origins</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elberfeld">Elberfeld</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erlangen">Erlangen</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.26,7.15&amp;year=1928" aria-label="Elberfeld on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Adolf Schulten"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5382 5724h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5382 5724h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.26,7.15&amp;year=1928">What was here in 1928? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
